--TEST--
An ungranted predicate is refused rather than answered `false`, and the denial unwinds out of two frames and through a `finally` to reach a `catch (Throwable)`, carrying a backtrace and no cause — `rule:security/denial-is-a-runtime-error`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:errors/capability-denials-are-catchable
// A predicate that answered `false` with the grant missing would leave an
// ungranted deployment looking like an empty one, and a check of the message
// cannot see that half of the rule.

final class Report
{
    public static function isOnDisk(): bool
    {
        return Core\IO::exists("report.txt");
    }

    public static function collect(): bool
    {
        try {
            return Report::isOnDisk();
        } finally {
            // The denial is a throw and nothing else, so the way out of this
            // frame is the way out of any other.
            echo "the finally ran\n";
        }
    }
}

try {
    echo Report::collect() ? "answered true\n" : "answered false\n";
} catch (Throwable $denied) {
    echo $denied is RuntimeError ? "class: RuntimeError\n" : "class: other\n";
    echo "frames: ", Core\Arr::count($denied->backtrace), "\n";
    echo $denied->previous == null ? "no cause\n" : "has a cause\n";
}

// The grant was the only thing missing: nothing was consumed and nothing was
// left behind, so the program goes on from the statement after the `catch`.
echo "still running\n";
--EXPECT--
the finally ran
class: RuntimeError
frames: 2
no cause
still running
